extended_information.full_description:
The [MCP TypeScript SDK](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk) implements the full MCP specification, making it easy to create MCP servers, build MCP clients and use standard transports like stdio and Streamable HTTP
It was found that the `UriTemplate.match()` function is susceptible to ReDoS due to a catastrophic backtracking when processing RFC 6570 URI template standard exploded array patterns, such as:

- Single Exploded: `{/id*}`, `{?tags*}`
- Complex Exploded: `{/path*}{?filter*}`
- Nested Exploded: `/api{/version*}/users{id*}`

The vulnerability can be exploited when processing URIs received by an untrusted source and passing them into the `UriTemplate.match()` function, or when processing the URI received in a request into `ResourceTemplate`. An example of a vulnerable snippet:

```
// Server registers this template
server.registerResource(
  "user-files",
  new ResourceTemplate("file:///users{/id*}/files{/path*}", { list: undefined }),
  { title: "User Files" },
  async (uri, variables, extra) => { /* ... */ }
);
// Attacker sends this request
client.readResource({
  uri: "file:///users/user1,user2,user3,user4,user5,user6,user7,suer8,user,9,user10,user11,user12,user13,user14,user16,user17,user18,user19,user20,FAIL/files/path1,path2,path3FAIL/"
});
```

extended_information.remediation:
##### Development mitigations

Explicitly enable DNS rebinding protection by setting `enableDnsRebindingProtection` to `true`.

For example, when creating an SSE-based MCP server -
```
const transport = new SSEServerTransport('/messages', mockRes, {
                        allowedHosts: ['localhost:3000', 'example.com'],
                        enableDnsRebindingProtection: true
                    });
```

